  "title": "utilpeek: kimchi and USDT premium (BTC, ETH, USDT on local exchanges vs the global price)"
 },
 "description": "utilpeek: Use when an agent needs to gauge local demand for crypto: the kimchi or USDT premium on local exchanges vs the global price. For global sentiment use get_crypto_fear_greed_index. Returns BTC, ETH and USDT on large local exchanges in KR, JP, ID, PH, TR, BR, MX and AR in USD, with each venue's premium to the global price and the FX source and date. Input: optional `asset` and `country`; both default to all. Last trades from public tickers, cached 30 s; references are Chainlink (BTC, ETH) and 1.0 (USDT); FX is the ECB daily fixing (BCRA for ARS), so under about 0.5 % is noise. Venue terms are unclear and each is credited. A failed venue is listed in `errors`; nothing priced is a 503 (not charged). Informational only, not investment advice. Typically under 0.5 s from cache; up to about 10 s when the venues are fetched. Price: USD 0.002. Free: 10 utilpeek calls per IP per UTC day. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/kimchi-premium-api.html",
